{"y":1992,"label":"1991–92","coach":"Jim Calhoun","conf":"Big East","confShort":"Big East","w":20,"l":10,"cw":10,"cl":8,"confFinish":"6th in Big East","finish":"r32","seed":9,"region":"Southeast","apPre":15,"apHigh":5,"srs":15.03,"sos":7.1,"ortg":101.6,"drtg":91.4,"ppg":79.0,"oppg":71.1,"story":{"headline":"Chris Smith Writes the Record Book","text":"Bridgeport's own Chris Smith closed his career as UConn's all-time leading scorer with 2,145 points, earning first-team All-Big East honors as a senior. The Huskies went 20–10 (10–8 Big East), beating No. 23 Wake Forest, No. 17 St. John's and No. 24 Syracuse along the way, while freshman Donyell Marshall made the Big East All-Freshman team and Scott Burrell was second-team All-Big East. St. John's knocked UConn out of the Big East tournament in overtime, 64–59, but the Huskies returned to the NCAA tournament and crushed Nebraska 86–65 before Ohio State ended the season 78–55 in the second round. Smith, who also left as the school's career leader in three-pointers with 242, was drafted 34th overall by the Minnesota Timberwolves.","moments":[{"date":"1992-03-19","title":"NCAA First Round: W vs Nebraska","text":"UConn beat Nebraska 86–65 in the NCAA tournament first round at Riverfront Coliseum, Cincinnati, Ohio."},{"date":"1992-03-21","title":"NCAA Second Round: L vs Ohio State","text":"UConn lost to Ohio State 55–78 in the NCAA tournament second round at Riverfront Coliseum, Cincinnati, Ohio."}],"honors":["Chris Smith – First-team All-Big East"],"sources":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1991%E2%80%9392_Connecticut_Huskies_men's_basketball_team","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UConn_Huskies_men%27s_basketball","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Smith_(basketball,_born_1970)"]},"roster":[{"pid":"chris-smith-1","name":"Chris Smith","num":"13","cls":"SR","pos":"G","ht":"6-3","wt":190,"home":"Bridgeport, CT","pg":{"g":30,"gs":30,"mp":36.3,"pts":21.2,"trb":3.3,"ast":3.7,"stl":1.2,"blk":0.5,"tov":2.8,"fg_pct":0.415,"fg3_pct":0